      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:de7f79b5cff35f611b3804132c5fd239b280c80bffe9928d4b889593a25576a2",
      "text": "Salesforce CDC payloads require two interpretations: Avro deserialization with the received event\u2019s schema, and change-header bitmap decoding. An UPDATE can include empty values for unchanged fields as well as fields cleared to null. changedFields and nulledFields distinguish those cases. Compound fields require nested bitmap handling, and diffFields identifies values delivered as diffs. These semantics matter when a Case alert depends on a specific field change. Schema caching must follow schema IDs, and compatibility depends on Avro resolution rules.",
